ADDENDA <Act No. 20277, Feb. 13, 2024>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation; provided, the following amended provisions shall enter into force on the dates specified in the relevant subparagraphs:
1. The amended provisions of Articles 5 (1) 21 through 24, the proviso of paragraph (2) 6 of that Article, and subparagraphs 9 and 14 of that paragraph: 3 months after the date of the promulgation;
2. The amended provisions of Article 8-7, the former part, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 31 (1), and subparagraph 7-2 of that paragraph: 6x months after the date of the promulgation.
Article 2 (Transitional measures regarding persons registered as patient suffering from potential aftereffects of defoliants)
(1) A person who falls under the categories specified in the amended provisions of Article 5 (1) 21 through 24, among persons who were determined and registered as patients suffering from potential aftereffects of defoliants as they fell under the categories specified in the previous provisions of the main clause of Article 5 (2) 6, Article 5 (2) 9, the main clause of subparagraph 12 of that paragraph, and subparagraph 14 of that paragraph before the enforcement date under subparagraph 1 of Article 1 of the Addenda, shall be deemed a person determined and registered as patients suffering from actual aftereffects of defoliants under this Act from the enforcement date under subparagraph 1 of Article 1 of the Addenda.
(2) A person who filed for registration as a patient suffering from potential aftereffects of defoliants before the enforcement date specified in subparagraph 1 of Article 1 of the Addenda on the grounds of progressive supranuclear palsy and multiple system atrophy among central nervous system disorders under the main clause of Article 5 (2) 6, multiple sclerosis under subparagraph 9 of that paragraph, bladder cancer among malignant tumors under the main clause of subparagraph 12 of that, or hypothyroidism under subparagraph 14 of that paragraph, shall be deemed to have filed for registration as a patient suffering from actual aftereffects of defoliants under the amended provisions of Article 5 (1) 21 through 24. In such cases, a physical examination under Article 6-2 shall include the joint determination of the veterans disability rating and the disability rating.
Article 3 (Transitional measures regarding compensation)
If a person who was registered or filed for registration, as a patient suffering from potential aftereffects of defoliants under the previous provisions of main clause of Article 5 (2) 6, subparagraph 9 of that paragraph, the main clause of subparagraph 12 of that paragraph, or subparagraph 14 of that paragraph before the enforcement date specified in subparagraph 1 of Article 1 of the Addenda, is classified as a patient suffering from actual aftereffects of defoliants under the amended provisions of Article 5 (1) 21 through 24 after the enforcement date specified in subparagraph 1 of Article 1 of the Addenda, compensation shall be paid to the person from the month in which the enforcement date specified in subparagraph 1 of Article 1 of the Addenda falls, notwithstanding Article 6 (4).
ADDENUM <Act No. 20683, Jan. 21, 2025>
This Act shall enter into force 3 months after the date of its promulgation.
